module main

# spec/todo.md item 20: an implicit-generic call's still-open result leaf
# could only be resolved by `check_interpolated_string`'s own retry queue
# (`pending_interp_segments_`), because `demand()` — the only way most
# expression positions (a binary operand, an index, a match subject) ask a
# subexpression for its concrete type — gave up on a leaf minted by
# `mint_open_result` instead of running `resolve_open_param_calls`/
# `finish_open_results` itself. `1 + add_one(5)` used to fail at lowering
# with "no concrete checked type is available for this node" while the same
# call under `"{add_one(5)}"` already worked.
def add_one(x):
    x + 1

def main() -> int32:
    println("{1 + add_one(5)}")
    return 0
